  condemned
  // Generic parked state. The other hold statuses each carry their own reason
  // implicitly (parts / approval / vendor); this one exists for the two reasons
  // that had no home — waiting on someone inside Basin, and everything else —
  // and is the ONLY status where holdReason must be supplied explicitly.
  on_hold
}

// Why a unit is parked, as shown on the board's On-Hold pill. Three of these
// are DERIVED from status and never stored (see services/shopHoldReason.ts):
// awaiting_parts -> waiting_parts, awaiting_approval -> waiting_customer_approval,
// outside_service/warranty_out -> external_vendor. Only waiting_internal and
// other are ever written to ShopWorkOrderItem.holdReason, and only alongside
// the on_hold status. Storing a derived value would let status and reason
// disagree; the derivation makes that unrepresentable.
/// WI-09 — what the CUSTOMER is charged for outside-vendor work.
///
/// Four values rather than the old `isWarranty` boolean, because three of them
/// are non-billable for three different reasons and the difference is the whole
/// point: "we ate this as goodwill" and "the vendor covered it under warranty"
/// and "this was our own gear" produce the same invoice and completely
/// different answers at the end of the quarter.
enum ShopVendorDisposition {
  /// Vendor covered it. Non-billable.
  warranty
  /// Bill the vendor's cost through to the customer (+ freight, + markup).
  pass_thru_repair
  /// We chose to eat it. Non-billable, and deliberately distinguishable from
  /// warranty so nobody later reports goodwill as vendor recovery.
  no_charge
  /// Basin's own equipment. Non-billable to a customer; the vendor cost is
  /// still recorded, as internal cost.
  internal
}

