// Billing Lineage & Mirrored Status (handoff: Billing Status Ownership and
// Ticket-to-Invoice Lineage). Rule 1: ServiceTicket owns exactly this one
// billing field. Everything QB/Enverus asserts lives in BillingObservation
// (mirror, never a bare column) — see that model below.
//
// `unclassified` is the pre-human-decision default (every ticket starts
// here) and is distinct from `not_billable` (a deliberate human call, always
// carrying a reason code + actor — see the CHECK constraint in the
// migration). The handoff's 4 states describe the classified states; this
// 5th one is the honest "nobody has looked at this yet" default the handoff
// didn't need to name because it assumed classification happens immediately.
enum BillingReadiness {
  unclassified // default; not yet classified by a human
  not_billable // requires billingReadinessReasonCode + billingReadinessSetById
  ready // human-set; requires serviceDate + signature if the billing profile requires one
  invoiced // set only by the derived-invoice process, never by hand
  submitted // set only by the OpenInvoice submission process, never by hand
}

